  "body": "## Summary\n- Resolves the recorded `open_decision` in the NECROMANCY `language_agnostic` doctrine in favor of option (a): a real multi-language parser (tree-sitter), reusing the existing language-neutral `classify_symbol` unchanged.\n- Adds `mantle/assimilator/scanner_ts.py`: a tree-sitter parser surface for `.js/.mjs/.go/.rs`, emitting the same `{symbol, kind, line, role}` records as the Python scanner.\n- `scan_project` now routes those extensions through `scanner_ts` when the optional tree-sitter stack is installed, and falls back to Python-only when it isn't \u2014 no behavior change for existing users.\n- Adds `examples/sample_app/notes_app.js`, a JS twin of `notes_app.py`, and `examples/tests/test_multilang_parity.py`, which asserts the JS organ map equals the Python organ map and checks the scan is read-only. The test skips cleanly if tree-sitter isn't installed.\n- Declares the dependency as an optional `multilang` extra in `pyproject.toml` (`pip install mantle-os[multilang]`).\n\nManually verified the classifier produces the exact organ distribution recorded as validated in the doctrine for the JS fixture: `{brain:1, heart:2, immune:2, limbs:2, memory:2, senses:1}` \u2014 matching the Python fixture exactly.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `python -m unittest examples.tests.test_multilang_parity` \u2014 passes (skips the tree-sitter-dependent cases in environments without the optional extra, since `tree_sitter_languages` doesn't yet ship wheels for newer Python versions)\n- [x] Manually confirmed `classify_symbol` + camelCase normalization produces identical organ counts to the validated Python baseline\n- [x] Confirmed `scan_project` without the optional dependency still returns `read_only: True` and unchanged `python_files` count (no behavior change for existing users)\n- [ ] CI / maintainer: run the parity test in an environment with `pip install mantle-os[multilang]` (tree-sitter 0.21.x requires Python <3.12) to exercise the tree-sitter path end-to-end\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
